          "capability": "Label all heart anatomy diagrams (external features, internal chambers, valve apparatus, major vessels, coronary circulation) in anterior/posterior/cross-sectional views; trace the complete systemic-to-pulmonary blood flow sequence through every chamber, valve, and vessel; solve NEET-level theory MCQs on cardiac conduction, cardiac cycle phases with pressure changes, heart sound-valve correlations, ECG wave-conduction mapping, cardiac output calculations, autonomic regulation effects, and high-yield clinical correlates (heart blocks, murmurs, coronary occlusion patterns).",
          "why_here": "All 25 in-play concepts form a single integrated NEET heart chapter. Anatomy concepts (gross, chambers, valves, vessels, coronary) build the structural foundation; blood flow sequence integrates them into the core construct target; physiology concepts (conduction, cycle, sounds, ECG, hemodynamics, autonomic, clinical) complete the theory coverage. They are taught together in NCERT, tested together in NEET, and depend on each other (flow needs anatomy; physiology needs flow/valves). One module matches the single-exam, single-sitting preparation context."
